your own decision and report it.

### What self-calibration bought (reported improvements)

| Gain reported | Paper |
|---|---|
| rms 36 to 16 mJy/beam (line-free), 100 to 18 mJy/beam (line); continuum rms ~40x; ~10x (3C138); 3.5-4x with line rms up to 30% | 2015ApJ...806...17R; 2017ApJ...851..132C; 2015ApJ...808L...1A; 2026A&A...711A.159M |
| dynamic range x11.4, x31.9, x57.7 to 11200 after phase, amp, amp+phase; ~380 to ~2860; ~120 to ~250 | 2017A&A...603A..68M; 2017NatAs...1..848V; 2020ApJ...892L..18I |
| peak S/N 150 to 1320; SNR x3.8; x1.8; 28 to 37 | 2014ApJ...791L...6W; 2021ApJ...923..121Y; 2018ApJ...859..111H; 2018MNRAS.475.4924K |
| line S/N +50% CO(1-0), +30% CO(3-2); x1.2 CO(1-0), none at CO(3-2); line self-cal x1.1-1.5 | 2018ApJ...863..193V; 2016ApJ...832..148V; 2019A&A...622A.206M |
| rms ~20%, 14%, ~25%, <=10%; S/N ~10% for peak S/N>20 targets | 2020ApJ...898...10T; 2018ApJ...865...13T; 2017Sci...355.1285N; 2017ApJ...838..114K; 2015ApJ...812...43B |
| ALMAGAL: 81% (7M), 66% (TM2), 45% (TM1) of eligible fields improved; Taurus disks: SNR x~1.5 at ~10 Mlambda max baseline, several times at ~2 Mlambda | 2025A&A...696A.150S; 2024PASJ...76..437Y |

These are individual case results with different metrics (image rms, peak S/N, dynamic range), not a validated
prediction by source brightness or morphology; compare like with like. Two sample-level results point the same
way: gains are smaller for more extended arrays (ALMAGAL success rate by array, 2025A&A...696A.150S; Taurus disk
SNR gain by maximum baseline, 2024PASJ...76..437Y).

